-e with an unset variable: report it, do not crash.

When the variable -e names is not set, sshpass reports it and then still
calls hide_password(), which copies args.orig_password -- NULL here -- and
dies with SIGSEGV instead of exiting with its "invalid arguments" status.
Only hide a password that exists.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -185,7 +185,8 @@
                 error=RETURN_INVALID_ARGUMENTS;
             }
 
-            hide_password();
+            if( args.orig_password!=NULL )
+                hide_password();
             unsetenv(optarg);
             break;
         case '?':
